  description="Practical information for Hersham residents: schools, doctors and pharmacies, getting around, and council services."
>
  <slot name="structured-data">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(hershamWebPage({
      path: '/hersham/living/',
      name: 'Living in Hersham',
      description: 'Practical information for Hersham residents: schools, doctors and pharmacies, getting around, and council services.',
    }))} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://walton-on-thames.org/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Hersham', item: 'https://walton-on-thames.org/hersham/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Living in Hersham', item: 'https://walton-on-thames.org/hersham/living/' },
      ],
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      mainEntity: faqs.map((item) => ({
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: item.q,
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
      })),
    })} />
  </slot>

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="breadcrumbs">
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/hersham/">Hersham</a></li>
          <li aria-current="page">Living in Hersham</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1>Living in Hersham</h1>
      <p>Schools, doctors, getting around and council services, for people who live in the village rather than visit it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <p>Hersham works as a village in a way its size does not guarantee. Three primary schools and a secondary sit within or immediately beside it, there is a GP surgery and two pharmacies by the green, and the station puts London Waterloo within a direct half-hour. What it does not have is a large shopping centre, a hospital, or its own council: for those, Hersham looks to Walton-on-Thames, Kingston and Elmbridge.</p>

        <blockquote>
          <p><strong>Reviewed {reviewedOn}.</strong> Schools, services and council arrangements change. Every entry below links to the organisation&rsquo;s own page, which is the current source.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2 id="schools">Schools</h2>
        <p>Three primary schools serve the village, along with one secondary immediately to its north.</p>

        {schools.map((school) => (
          <div class="entry">
            <h3>{school.name}</h3>
            <p class="entry-address">{school.address}</p>
            <p>{school.detail}</p>
            <p class="entry-links">
              <a href={school.site} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">School website &#8599;</a>
              <a href={school.ofsted} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ofsted record &#8599;</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        ))}

        <h3>A note on Ofsted ratings</h3>
        <p>We link to each school&rsquo;s Ofsted record rather than repeating a rating here, and that is deliberate. Inspections of these four schools span more than a decade, so any single word would be undated. More importantly, <strong>Ofsted stopped making an overall effectiveness judgement for state-funded schools in September 2024</strong>. Schools inspected since then receive grades in separate categories with no headline verdict, which means an older &ldquo;Good&rdquo; and a newer one are not describing the same thing. Read the report rather than the label.</p>
        <p>Admissions, catchment areas and appeals are handled by Surrey County Council, not by the schools or the borough. See <a href="https://www.surreycc.gov.uk/schools-and-learning/schools/admissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surrey County Council school admissions &#8599;</a>. For the wider picture across the borough, see our <a href="/living/schools/">schools guide</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="health">Doctors, dentists and pharmacies</h2>
        <p>Hersham has its own GP surgery and two pharmacies, both by the green, plus two dental practices. Full details and opening arrangements are on each listing.</p>
        <ul>
          {health.map((item) => (
            <li><a href={item.href}>{item.name}</a> &mdash; {item.what}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p>The nearest major hospitals are outside the village. For borough-wide lists see our guides to <a href="/living/gp-surgeries/">GP surgeries</a>, <a href="/living/pharmacies/">pharmacies</a> and <a href="/living/dentists/">dentists</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="getting-around">Getting around</h2>
        <p>Hersham station sits on the South West Main Line with direct trains to London Waterloo, and is the main reason the village works as a commuter base. Walton-on-Thames station also serves the west of the village and has more frequent services; both are covered in our <a href="/hersham-railway-station/">Hersham station guide</a> and <a href="/walton-on-thames-railway-station/">Walton-on-Thames station guide</a>.</p>
        <p>By road, the A244 runs through the village between Esher and Walton, and the A317 links west towards Weybridge. The M25 is a few miles east at Junction 10.</p>
        <p>Buses serve the village and connect it to Walton, Esher, Kingston and Cobham, but route numbers and operators change often enough that listing them here would go stale. Surrey County Council publishes current routes and timetables: see <a href="https://www.surreycc.gov.uk/roads-and-transport/buses-and-trains" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surrey County Council buses and trains &#8599;</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="council">Council services</h2>
        <p>Two councils currently cover Hersham, and residents regularly contact the wrong one.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Elmbridge Borough Council</strong> handles bin collections, council tax, parking, licensing and planning applications. <a href="https://www.elmbridge.gov.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">elmbridge.gov.uk &#8599;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Surrey County Council</strong> handles schools and admissions, highways and roadworks, adult social care, children&rsquo;s services and libraries. <a href="https://www.surreycc.gov.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">surreycc.gov.uk &#8599;</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>That split ends soon. On <strong>1 April 2027</strong> both are replaced by <strong>East Surrey Council</strong>, a single unitary authority also covering Epsom and Ewell, Mole Valley, Reigate and Banstead, and Tandridge, which will take on borough and county functions together. Shadow authority elections were held in May 2026. Until the handover, contact the councils as now.</p>
        <p>For what is being built around the village, and how to comment on an application, see <a href="/hersham/development-and-planning/">development and planning in Hersham</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="everyday">Shops and everyday needs</h2>
        <p>The parade around Hersham Green carries the village&rsquo;s everyday shopping, with a supermarket, cafes and takeaways alongside the pharmacy and post office.</p>
        <ul>
          {everyday.map((item) => (
            <li><a href={item.href}>{item.name}</a> &mdash; {item.what}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p>For eating and drinking, see <a href="/hersham/food-and-drink/">food and drink in Hersham</a>. For everything else, the <a href="/directory/">business directory</a> lists Hersham businesses alongside the rest of the area.</p>

        <h2 id="green-space">Parks and green space</h2>
        <p>Two recreation grounds serve the village: <a href="/things-to-do/hersham-recreation-ground/">Hersham Recreation Ground</a>, which has a play area and a seasonal splash pad, and <a href="/things-to-do/coronation-recreation-ground-hersham/">Coronation Recreation Ground</a>, with a play area, sports pitches and a cafe. <a href="/hersham/hersham-green/">Hersham Green</a> itself hosts events through the year, and the <a href="/hersham/river-mole-walks/">River Mole walks</a> start within a few minutes of the built-up centre.</p>

        <h2 id="faqs">Common questions</h2>
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <>
            <h3>{item.q}</h3>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </>
        ))}

        <p>For the village more widely, see the <a href="/hersham/">Hersham guide</a>, <a href="/things-to-do/hersham/">things to do in Hersham</a> and <a href="/hersham/history/">Hersham&rsquo;s history</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

